<title>BELGIUM: New listings boost market cap on Brussels bourse.</title>
<headline>New listings boost market cap on Brussels bourse.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brussels Stock Exchange said on Friday 23 billion Belgian francs ($637 million) was raised on the capital market via an unusually high number of new listings in June.</p>
<p>New additions included shares in Brantano, Hamon, GIMV and Ipso-ILG.</p>
<p>&quot;This significant increase in the number of listed companies boosted market capitalization to 4,896.93 billion francs at the end of June, a 6.25 percent rise over the previous month's level,&quot; the bourse said.</p>
<p>Total volume in June was 122.63 billion, the highest ever. A 1997 record was set on June 20 when maturing futures and options contracts on the Bel-20 index  .BFX pushed up the day's volume to 15.6 billion, the highest since February 1988.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710 ($ = 36.12 Belgian Francs)</p>
